  "fixed_contract_lean": "import Mathlib\n\n/- Effect-additive Busch-type inputs; not a Gleason proof. -/\nnamespace BornFable\n\nstructure OrderedQUnit (V : Type*) [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℚ V] where\n  le : V → V → Prop\n  le_refl : ∀ x, le x x\n  le_trans : ∀ x y z, le x y → le y z → le x z\n  add_le_add_right : ∀ x y z, le x y → le (x + z) (y + z)\n  smul_nonneg : ∀ (q : ℚ) (x : V), 0 ≤ q → le 0 x → le 0 (q • x)\n  u : V\n  u_nonneg : le 0 u\n\nvariable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module ℚ V]\n\ndef OrderedQUnit.Effect (S : OrderedQUnit V) (a : V) : Prop := S.le 0 a ∧ S.le a S.u\n\nstructure EffectValuation (S : OrderedQUnit V) where\n  v : V → ℚ\n  unit : v S.u = 1\n  nonneg : ∀ a, S.Effect a → 0 ≤ v a\n  additive : ∀ a b, S.Effect a → S.Effect b → S.Effect (a + b) → v (a + b) = v a + v b\n\n\nend BornFable\n",
  "frozen_target_types": "theorem val_zero (S : OrderedQUnit V) (W : EffectValuation S) : W.v 0 = 0\n\ntheorem effect_sub (S : OrderedQUnit V) {a b : V} (ha : S.Effect a) (hb : S.Effect b) (hab : S.le a b) : S.Effect (b - a)\n\ntheorem val_mono (S : OrderedQUnit V) (W : EffectValuation S) {a b : V} (ha : S.Effect a) (hb : S.Effect b) (hab : S.le a b) : W.v a ≤ W.v b\n\ntheorem val_le_one (S : OrderedQUnit V) (W : EffectValuation S) {a : V} (ha : S.Effect a) : W.v a ≤ 1\n\ntheorem effect_smul (S : OrderedQUnit V) {a : V} (q : ℚ) (hq0 : 0 ≤ q) (hq1 : q ≤ 1) (ha : S.Effect a) : S.Effect (q • a)\n\ntheorem val_nsmul (S : OrderedQUnit V) (W : EffectValuation S) {a : V} (k : ℕ) (ha : S.Effect a) (hka : S.Effect ((k : ℚ) • a)) : W.v ((k : ℚ) • a) = (k : ℚ) * W.v a\n\ntheorem val_rat_smul (S : OrderedQUnit V) (W : EffectValuation S) {a : V} (q : ℚ) (hq0 : 0 ≤ q) (hq1 : q ≤ 1) (ha : S.Effect a) : W.v (q • a) = q * W.v a\n\ntheorem val_sandwich (S : OrderedQUnit V) (W : EffectValuation S) {a b : V} (ha : S.Effect a) (hb : S.Effect b) (ε : ℚ) (hε0 : 0 ≤ ε) (hε1 : ε ≤ 1) (hlo : S.le (-(ε • S.u)) (a - b)) (hhi : S.le (a - b) (ε • S.u)) : -ε ≤ W.v a - W.v b ∧ W.v a - W.v b ≤ ε\n",
  "p0_claims_for_derivation": [
    {
      "n": 1,
      "statement": "Order facts in Setting S. For all x, y, z ∈ V, q ∈ ℚ: (F1) x ≤ y ⟺ 0 ≤ y − x; (F2) 0 ≤ x and 0 ≤ y ⟹ 0 ≤ x + y; (F3) x ≤ y and 0 ≤ q ⟹ q·x ≤ q·y; (F5) 0 ≤ a and 0 ≤ p ≤ q (p, q ∈ ℚ) ⟹ p·a ≤ q·a.",
      "proof": "(F1) Apply (O1) with z = −x to x ≤ y to get 0 ≤ y − x; conversely apply (O1) with z = x to 0 ≤ y − x. (F2) From 0 ≤ x and (O1) with z = y: y ≤ x + y; transitivity with 0 ≤ y. (F3) By (F1), 0 ≤ y − x; by (O2), 0 ≤ q·(y − x) = q·y − q·x; by (F1), q·x ≤ q·y. (F5) q·a − p·a = (q − p)·a with q − p ≥ 0 and a ≥ 0, so 0 ≤ (q − p)·a by (O2); conclude by (F1)."
    },
    {
      "n": 2,
      "statement": "(L1) v(0) = 0.",
      "proof": "0 ∈ E since 0 ≤ 0 (reflexivity) and 0 ≤ u. The pair (0,0) is summable with sum 0 ∈ E, so by (A3) v(0) = v(0) + v(0), hence v(0) = 0 in the ordered field W."
    },
    {
      "n": 3,
      "statement": "(L2) If a, b ∈ E and a ≤ b then b − a ∈ E, b = a + (b − a), and v(a) ≤ v(b). Consequently 0 ≤ v(a) ≤ 1 for all a ∈ E.",
      "proof": "0 ≤ b − a by (F1). Since b − (b − a) = a ≥ 0, (F1) gives b − a ≤ b, and b ≤ u, so b − a ≤ u by transitivity; thus b − a ∈ E. The pair (a, b − a) is summable with sum b ∈ E, so (A3) gives v(b) = v(a) + v(b − a) ≥ v(a) by (A2). The bound 0 ≤ v(a) ≤ v(u) = 1 follows from (A2), a ≤ u, and (A1)."
    },
    {
      "n": 4,
      "statement": "(L4) If a ∈ E, k ∈ ℕ and k·a ∈ E, then v(k·a) = k·v(a).",
      "proof": "Induction on k. k = 0: v(0) = 0 by Claim 2. Step: assume (k+1)·a ∈ E. Then k·a ∈ E: 0 ≤ k·a by (O2); k·a ≤ (k+1)·a by (F5) (a ≥ 0, k ≤ k+1); (k+1)·a ≤ u; transitivity. The pair (k·a, a) is summable with sum (k+1)·a ∈ E, so (A3) and the induction hypothesis (applicable since k·a ∈ E) give v((k+1)·a) = v(k·a) + v(a) = k·v(a) + v(a) = (k+1)·v(a)."
    },
    {
      "n": 5,
      "statement": "(L5) If a ∈ E and q ∈ ℚ with 0 ≤ q ≤ 1, then q·a ∈ E and v(q·a) = q·v(a).",
      "proof": "Write q = m/n with n ≥ 1 and 0 ≤ m ≤ n naturals (numerator and denominator; m ≤ n because q ≤ 1). Put b := (1/n)·a. Then 0 ≤ b by (O2), b ≤ a by (F5) (1/n ≤ 1), a ≤ u; so b ∈ E. Since n·b = a ∈ E, Claim 4 gives v(a) = n·v(b). Also m·b = q·a with 0 ≤ m·b ≤ n·b = a ≤ u by (O2) and (F5), so m·b ∈ E and Claim 4 gives v(q·a) = v(m·b) = m·v(b) = (m/n)·v(a) = q·v(a). Note that only (A3) was used."
    },
    {
      "n": 6,
      "statement": "(L6, order-unit sandwich bound) Let a, b ∈ E and ε ∈ ℚ with 0 ≤ ε ≤ 1. If −ε·u ≤ a − b ≤ ε·u then −ε ≤ v(a) − v(b) ≤ ε. No linearity or quadratic form of v is assumed.",
      "proof": "Set d := a − b + ε·u and d' := (1/2)·d. From −ε·u ≤ a − b and (F1): 0 ≤ d. From a − b ≤ ε·u and (O1) (add ε·u): d ≤ 2ε·u. By (F3) with q = 1/2: 0 ≤ d' and d' ≤ ε·u; by (F5) (ε ≤ 1, u ≥ 0): ε·u ≤ u. Hence d' ∈ E and ε·u ∈ E, with d' ≤ ε·u. Set s := (1/2)·a + (ε/2)·u. In the ℚ-module V, (1/2)·b + d' = (1/2)·(b + a − b + ε·u) = s. Membership: (1/2)·a, (1/2)·b, (ε/2)·u ∈ E by Claim 5 (scalars in ℚ ∩ [0,1]). s ∈ E: 0 ≤ s by (F2); (1/2)·a ≤ (1/2)·u by (F3), (ε/2)·u ≤ (1/2)·u by (F5), so by (O1) twice and transitivity s ≤ (1/2)·u + (1/2)·u = u. Therefore both pairs ((1/2)·a, (ε/2)·u) and ((1/2)·b, d') are summable with the same sum s, and (A3) gives v((1/2)·a) + v((ε/2)·u) = v(s) = v((1/2)·b) + v(d'). By Claim 5: v((1/2)·a) = v(a)/2, v((1/2)·b) = v(b)/2, v((ε/2)·u) = (ε/2)·v(u) = ε/2. By Claim 3 and Claim 5: 0 ≤ v(d') ≤ v(ε·u) = ε·v(u) = ε (the lower bound is (A2)). Hence v(a)/2 + ε/2 = v(b)/2 + v(d'), i.e. v(a) − v(b) = 2·v(d') − ε ∈ [−ε, ε]."
    }
  ],
  "output_contract": "Return ONE JSON object with exact binding fields, candidate_certificate (schema in answer_schema), construction (target declarations), remaining_obligations, operad_delta with six arrays, claim_boundary. lean_proof_body is declarations/proofs ONLY, inserted INSIDE namespace BornFable after contract.lean. No imports, namespaces, end namespace, custom axioms, sorry, admit, native_decide, unsafe, IO, macros, or notation/instance redefinitions. No altered contract structures. Helpers allowed. Supply real Lean proofs of all eight targets, no plan/placeholders. Host appends independent frozen-type wrappers. Use imported Mathlib. Do not claim compilation. Numeric outputs are canonical rational strings and actual booleans. Keep this unit bounded; no re-mining or trace-representation attempt."
}
